X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/second-annual-institute-on-spirituality-building-interfaith-community-dialogue-and-action-for-social-change"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261010T052518Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54045314627157
DTSTART:20261009T130000Z
DTEND:20261009T203000Z
DESCRIPTION:Faith communities\, spiritual traditions and the helping profes
 sions all carry powerful resources for connection\, meaning and community.
  At a time when many people feel isolated\, overwhelmed or divided by poli
 tical\, social and religious conflict\, this institute will explore how pr
 actitioners\, community leaders and faith-based organizations can move fro
 m shared values to collective action.\n\nThe UNC School of Social Work is 
 hosting its second annual institute on spirituality for public health prof
 essionals\, scholars and practitioners on Friday\, Oct. 9.\n\n“Building 
 Interfaith Community: Dialogue and Action for Social Change” will featur
 e a keynote address from Pamela Ayo Yetunde\, co-founder of Buddhist Justi
 ce Reporter and the Year of the Black Woman Spiritual Direction program\, 
 as well as the author of several books.\n\nThe institute will bring togeth
 er social workers\, mental health providers\, chaplains\, clergy\, spiritu
 al care providers\, public health professionals\, students and community l
 eaders to examine common threads across spiritual and religious traditions
 : connection to something beyond the self\, connection to other people and
  responsibility to the wider community.
GEO:35.907113;-79.054241
LOCATION:UNC School of Social Work\, Tate-Turner-Kuralt Auditorium
SUMMARY:Second Annual Institute on Spirituality: Building Interfaith Commun
 ity: Dialogue and Action for Social Change
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/second-annual-institute-on-spi
 rituality-building-interfaith-community-dialogue-and-action-for-social-cha
 nge
CATEGORIES:Academic Calendar
END:VEVENT
