DESCRIPTION:Join us for the Ackland Art Museum’s fifth annual Acktoberfes
 t — an evening filled with art\, crafts\, and local vendors! \nArt suppl
 ies will be available in our ART& space\, where visitors can create their 
 own paper plants inspired by Phaan Howng: Against Nature. There will also 
 be postcards inspired by the installation for visitors to enjoy and use. \
 nExplore our special exhibitions Care and Concern: Recent Acquisitions of 
 Modern and Contemporary Art \, and Continental Shift: Recent Acquisitions 
 of African Art throughout the evening with extended museum hours. \nLocal 
 vendors will be on hand with goods to browse and purchase\, including Ding
 o Dog Brewing Company\, where visitors can grab a drink to sip while craft
 ing. \nAcktoberfest is a free\, walk-in program\; no registration required
  to attend or craft. Museum galleries will be open from 5–9 p.m.\; the v
 endors will be onsite from 6–8:30 p.m. \nOur vendors: \nDingo Dog Brewin
 g  \nFlower of Carolina \nNailah’s Shea \nStudent Made UNC \nWord and Pl
 ant \nBEAM
GEO:35.912593;-79.054867
LOCATION:Ackland Art Museum
SUMMARY:2nd Friday ArtWalk: Acktoberfest
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/2nd-friday-artwalk-acktoberfes
 t-6870
CATEGORIES:Exhibits
END:VEVENT
