SUMMARY:B19 Ride\, 50+ miles\, 19-20 mph
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T080500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T110500
DTSTAMP:20261010T053329Z
UID:event_316635042@meetup.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T080500
SEQUENCE:1
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261004T000958Z
DESCRIPTION:Carolina Tarwheels Cycling Club\nGoal is a brisk **group** rid
 e\, maintaining an organized pace line\, going easy on the climbs and spee
 ding up on the descents and communicating potential hazards to the group.\
 n\nRoute: Route to be published by Thursday @ 8 PM\n\nYour responsibility 
 as part of the group is to RSVP and supply your own cue sheet or download 
 the GPS file. **RSVP is required.** If you plan to join the ride in progre
 ss\, leave a comment below on where we can expect to meet you.\n\n**NOTE!*
 *\nThis is NOT a no-drop ride. All riders are expected to be skilled and e
 xperienced in SAFE pace line riding and capable of maintaining an average 
 pace of 19-20 mph. **The ride is limited to 20 riders.** We may split the 
 group into two smaller groups\, depending on how many show up.\n\nIt is Ta
 rwheels policy for all riders to sign the ride waiver before coming out to
  the ride.\n\n\\*\\*\\* WAIVER \\*\\*\\* [http://tarwheels.net/ewaiver](ht
 tp://tarwheels.net/ewaiver)\n\nMEMBERS need only do this ONCE a YEAR. NON-
 MEMBERS are required to do this before EACH RIDE\, please consider becomin
 g a member.\n\nPlease consult the Tarwheels website for Ride policies ([ht
 tp://tarwheels.net/wp/policies/](http://tarwheels.net/wp/policies/)) and t
 he BikeWalkNC website for guidance on riding in pacelines. Group Bicycling
  Best Practices: Skills and Techniques ([http://www.bikewalknc.org/group-b
 icycling-best-practices-skills-and-techniques/](http://www.bikewalknc.org/
 group-bicycling-best-practices-skills-and-techniques/)).
LAST-MODIFIED:20261004T000959Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://www.meetup.com/tarwheels/events/316635042/
X-SOURCE:Triangle Cycling
END:VEVENT
