DESCRIPTION:FEATURING\n\nKelariz Keshavarz\, flute\nSuzanne Polak\, piano\n
 Luke Ellard\, clarinet\nJessica Kunttu\, bassoon\nJeanne Fischer\, voice\n
 Heidi Radtke\, saxophone\nBrian Seaton\, English horn\n\n \n\nABOUT THE PR
 OGRAM\n\nIn celebration of the 250th anniversary of the United States\, th
 is chamber music concert brings together UNC faculty and guest artists to 
 celebrate the creativity and contributions of American women composers. Fe
 aturing works for flute in a variety of chamber settings\, the program hig
 hlights the breadth and diversity of American chamber music across generat
 ions.\n\n \n\nProgram\n\nJennifer Higdon Song (1995)\nfor solo flute\n\n \
 n\nAmy Beach Three Compositions\, Op. 40 (1898)\nfor flute and piano\n\n \
 n\nValerie Coleman Rubispheres (2012)\nfor flute\, clarinet\, and bassoon\
 n\n \n\nIntermission\n\n \n\nKatherine Hoover Seven Haiku (1973)\nfor flut
 e and voice\n\n \n\nCatherine Rollin Suite Detroit (2018)\nfor flute\, sax
 ophone\, and piano\n\n \n\nAmanda Harberg Crossroads (2022)\nfor flute\, E
 nglish horn\, and piano\n\n \n\nPARKING\n\nPlease plan to arrive early as 
 parking on campus can be tricky. Learn more about parking and directions t
 o UNC-Chapel Hill’s campus.
LOCATION:Hill Hall\, Moeser Auditorium
SUMMARY:Flute+: American Female Composers Night
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/flute-chamber-music-faculty-re
 cital
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
