DESCRIPTION:Ready to take your grant writing skills to the next level? Join
  us in-person for Navigating the Grant Writing Journey: From Idea to Succe
 ssful (Re)Submission.\n\n \n\nThis practical three-part workshop series co
 vers all aspects of preparing applications for external funding\, with a f
 ocus on NIH applications.\n\n \n\nThe three workshops will cover:\n\nGener
 al & strategic grantsmanshipEffective communicationSpecific Aims & Researc
 h StrategyBudgeting & supporting documentsReview and resubmission processI
 nteractive roundtable discussion \n\nThe three sessions are designed to bu
 ild on one another and cover the grant writing process as a whole. We enco
 urage you to register with attending all three sessions in mind.\n\n \n\n 
 \n\nSessions\n\n10/14/2026 (2-5 p.m.): Effective Communication\, General G
 rantsmanship\, and Specific Aims\n10/21/2026 (2-5 p.m.): Research Strategy
 \, Supporting Documents\, and Grant Review and Resubmissions\n10/28/2026 (
 2-5 p.m.): Budgeting for Grand Proposals\, Strategy & Grantsmanship\, and 
 Roundtable Discussion\n\n \n\nRegister\n\n \n\nFeatured Speakers\n\nSamant
 ha Schwartz\, PhD – Science Grant Writer\, NC TraCS InstituteNate Warren
 \, PhD – Research Development Manager\, UNC Office of Research Developme
 nt (ORD)Marina Sokolsky-Papkov\, PhD – Associate Professor\, DPMP\, UNC 
 Eshelman School of Pharmacy\; Director\, Translational Nanocharacterizatio
 n and Nanoformulation Research Laboratory\, Center for Nanotechnology in D
 rug DeliveryRebecca Carlson\, MLS\, AHIP – Health Sciences Librarian and
  liaison to the UNC Eshelman School of PharmacyKatherine Howell\, MSLIS 
 – Health Sciences LibrarianAmy Fry\, BA – Carolina Cancer Nanotechnolo
 gy T32 Training Program Coordinator and Grants Manager\, Office of Researc
 h Administration\, UNC Eshelman School of PharmacyTim Flood\, PhD – Clin
 ical Associate Professor of Management and Corporate Communication\, UNC K
 enan-Flagler Business SchoolAlan Marsh\, PhD – Associate Director\, Offi
 ce of Postdoctoral AffairsNathan Blouin\, MBA\, CRA – Assistant Vice Cha
 ncellor for Research DevelopmentJason Franz\, PhD – F32 Study Section Re
 viewer\; Professor\, Lampe Joint Department of Biomedical Engineering (UNC
  / NC State) \n\nQuestions? Contact Amy Fry at amy_fry@unc.edu\n\n \n\nPre
 sented by: Carolina Cancer Nanotechnology Training Program (C-CNTP) and th
 e NC Translational and Clinical Sciences (NC TraCS) Institute
GEO:35.907992;-79.051904
LOCATION:Wilson Hall\, Room 0128
SUMMARY:Navigating the Grant Writing Journey: From Idea to Successful (Re)S
 ubmission
