X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Yogainnaturenc": "https://www.meetup.com/yogainnaturenc/events/316077182/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_yogainnaturenc
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Yoga In Nature NC
UID:event_316077182@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T053309Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T110000
SUMMARY:Yoga In Nature™ FALL YOGA EVENT at For Garden's Sake
DESCRIPTION:Yoga In Nature™\, NC\n**Another fun Fall Yoga In Nature™\,
  NC event!!!** \\*\\*We will be joining For Garden's Sake (garden center) 
 for another seasonal yoga event and **FALL THEME** **“Harvesting\, trans
 itioning and making room for new growth.”** **$25/person paid in advance
 \, at sign up\, to secure your spot.** \\*\\*\\*Pay by Venmo @Darlene-Gena
 nder (0862 if asked for 4 digits) or by PayPal dgenander@yogainnature.com 
 Also accepting Zelle.\n\n\\*\\*BACK AGAIN BY POPULAR DEMAND...\\*\\*ALL TH
 INGS FALL!!! Come join us for a 60 minute vinyasa flow to yin practice for
  ALL LEVELS (as well as first timers). We will gather as a community in a 
 yoga practice that will focus on flowing with our breath as we move our bo
 dies and connect with nature. (No experience necessary\, just an open mind
 :) Theme of this Fall event: *“Harvesting\, transitioning and making roo
 m for new growth.”* Stay for hot seasonal tea. Receive a small seasonal 
 gift!!!\n\nBring a friend! Gift someone special who loves yoga and/or plan
 ts. NOTE THAT FOR GARDEN SAKE WILL BE DECORATED WITH FALL DECOR\, for insp
 iration. Wander the grounds of the garden center's indoor and outdoor plan
 ts\, shrubs and trees. Also\, take a look at their potting shed and visit 
 with the goats and ducks on the property.\n\nBring your own yoga mat and/o
 r towel\, water bottle\, and whatever you may need for your practice.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/yogainnaturenc/events/316077182/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260811T213749Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260811T213749Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncbg": "https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/autumn-forest-bathing-walk/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncbg
X-SOURCE:NC Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T120000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001642Z
CREATED:20261006T001501Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001642Z
UID:10000871-1792229400-1792238400@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Autumn Forest Bathing Walk
DESCRIPTION:with Aimee Vandemark\, Certified Forest and Nature Therapy Guide \nForest Therapy (sometimes known as Forest Bathing or Shinrin-Yoku) broadly means taking in the forest atmosphere with all of one’s senses. Not simply a walk in the woods; it is the conscious and contemplative practice of being immersed in the sights\, sounds\, and smells of the forest. During your walk\, Aimee Vandemark will guide you through invitations to awaken your senses\, slow down\, be present\, and reconnect with the nature and rhythm of your surroundings. Minimum Age: 18 \nREGISTER HERE \nRegistration is managed by the program leader. \nRegistration deadline: Friday\, October 16 at 10 a.m.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/autumn-forest-bathing-walk/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Health and Wellbeing
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=North Carolina Botanical Garden 100 Old Mason Farm Road Chapel Hill NC 27517 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=100 Old Mason Farm Road:geo:-79.031939,35.901081
END:VEVENT
