BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_newhopeaudubon
SUMMARY:Chapel Hill Bird Club Bird Outing
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T110000
DTSTAMP:20261010T053326Z
UID:0ni1geo1ofkjdkpa3ce29c51tr@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T080000
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20260926T013716Z
DESCRIPTION:Contact Bruce Young at <a href="mailto:byoung715@yahoo.com" t
 arget="_blank">byoung715@yahoo.com</a> for questions. The location will be
  Ebenezer Point\, Jordan Lake. Ebenezer is 2.3 miles south of Hwy. 64 on B
 eaver Creek Road (SR1008) on the east side of Jordan lake. There's a well-
 marked entrance on the right. More information\, including map coordinates
 \, is here: <a href="https://tbg.carolinanature.com/ebenezer.html">https:/
 /tbg.carolinanature.com/ebenezer.html</a><br><br>This outing is sponsored 
 by Chapel Hill Bird Club. More info about this outing is available at:  
 <a href="https://chbc.carolinanature.com/birdwalks/" target="_blank"><u><u
 >https://chbc.carolinanature.com/birdwalks/</u></u></a>.<br><br>Outings us
 ually last 2-3 hours. No reservations or sign-up needed. If there is a lar
 ge turnout for any particular outing\, we may split into two groups. We do
  recommend carpooling for families or friend pods\; while we love pets\, t
 here is a ‘no-pet’ policy for bird outings. New birders and birders of
  all skill levels are welcome. <br><br>Please wear long pants\, socks\, a
 nd sturdy shoes (ticks and chiggers may be present). Sun and bug protectio
 n are also recommended. Bring snacks and water if you like. Heavy rain wil
 l result in cancellation.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002T235449Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:New Hope Bird Alliance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/the-afterlife-of-trees-davidson/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T130000
DTSTAMP:20260824T161700Z
CREATED:20260824T161659Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260824T161700Z
UID:10001761-1792314000-1792328400@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:The Afterlife of Trees (Davidson)
DESCRIPTION:Dead trees are full of life! Join us at Fisher Farm for an in-person workshop on the critical role standing dead trees or “snags” play in providing vital wildlife habitat and supporting forest biodiversity. Learn how snags support wildlife as well as how to create them on your own property. Participants will get hands-on experience selecting ideal snag trees and various methods for creating them. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/the-afterlife-of-trees-davidson/
CATEGORIES:Featured
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/bass-lake-park-garden-planting-day-holly-springs/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T120000
DTSTAMP:20260909T175523Z
CREATED:20260909T175522Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T175523Z
UID:10001798-1792317600-1792324800@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Bass Lake Park Garden Planting Day (Holly Springs)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF South Wake Conservationists Chapter for a volunteer work day at our shade pollinator garden at Bass Lake Park! We’ll be getting the garden ready for the cooler months with a mix of seasonal maintenance and new planting. Volunteer activities will include garden cleanup and weeding\, installing new native shrubs and perennials\, and applying a final layer of mulch before winter. \nNo special experience is needed! We’ll have tools available to borrow\, but volunteers are encouraged to bring gloves\, sunscreen\, bug spray\, water\, and any favorite garden tools you’d like to use. Come spend some time outside\, meet fellow conservation-minded neighbors\, and help us continue building valuable pollinator habitat right here in our community. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/bass-lake-park-garden-planting-day-holly-springs/
CATEGORIES:Featured
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/invasive-plant-removal-matthews-4/"}
