BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-for-research-workflows"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261010T052518Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54126265418672
DTSTART:20261020T130000Z
DTEND:20261020T143000Z
DESCRIPTION:Generative AI is becoming part of many everyday research workfl
 ows\, from exploring a topic and evaluating information to organizing data
  and developing reports. In this hands-on workshop\, staff from the Librar
 y AI Studio will introduce practical ways to use generative AI to support 
 research-related tasks.\n\nParticipants will explore how to:\n\nUse genera
 tive AI to begin researching a topic and refine questionsEvaluate AI tools
  and choose appropriate models for different tasksIdentify misinformation\
 , inaccuracies\, and other limitations of AI-generated contentOrganize\, a
 nalyze\, and manipulate data with AI-supported toolsUse AI to assist with 
 report development and communicationMake informed decisions about when and
  how to incorporate AI into a research workflowThis workshop focuses on ac
 cessible\, practical applications rather than advanced or specialized rese
 arch computing. No prior experience with generative AI is required. Partic
 ipants will have opportunities to try tools and apply strategies to their 
 own research or information-related projects.
GEO:35.914361;-79.054904
LOCATION:Innovate Carolina Junction
SUMMARY:AI for Research Workflows
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-for-research-workflows
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
