DESCRIPTION:Join us for a conversation with David Crabtree\, CEO of PBS Nor
 th Carolina. Crabtree will explore the role public broadcast television pl
 ans in telling visual stories rooted in state and national history. Hosted
  by North Carolina-based podcaster Michael A. Betts II\, the discussion wi
 ll spotlight shows such as NC Weekend\, which features historic revolution
 ary sites across the state\, as well as the nationally acclaimed Ken Burns
  series\, The American Revolution\, in which Carolina's own Katlhleen DuVa
 l is featured prominently. The conversation will highlight the power of do
 cumentary film and television as an educational tool to engage citizens ac
 ross the state and nation in our collective story.
GEO:35.90984;-79.050769
LOCATION:Wilson Library \, Pleasants Family Assembly Room 
SUMMARY:A Conversation with PBS North Carolina CEO David Crabtree
