DTSTAMP:20261010T052518Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53665393335586
DTSTART:20261020T200000Z
DTEND:20261020T213000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the Three Minute Thesis Finals\, where the 10 gradu
 ate student finalists will compete to present their cutting-edge research 
 in just three minutes! Finals will be live\, in-person at Sonja Haynes Sto
 ne Center in the Hitchcock Multipurpose Room on October 20 at 4 p.m.\n \n\
 n\n\nThree Minute Thesis (3MT) is an academic competition in which partici
 pants have just three minutes to explain the breadth and significance of t
 heir research project to a non-specialist audience. It is designed to assi
 st graduate students with fostering effective presentation and communicati
 on skills. This event is the final round of the competition\, featuring 10
  graduate student presentations.\n \n\n\n\nThe winner will receive a $1000
  prize and the opportunity to represent UNC-Chapel Hill at the 3MT competi
 tion in Baton Rouge\, LA\, Feb. 18-20\, 2026 as part of the Conference of 
 Southern Graduate Schools annual conference. The “People’s choice” p
 rize will be awarded to a finalist chosen by the audience.
GEO:35.907852;-79.050272
LOCATION:The Sonja Haynes Stone Center for Research in Black Culture and Hi
 story\, Hitchcock Multipurpose Room
SUMMARY:2026 Three Minute Thesis Finals
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/2026-three-minute-thesis-final
 s
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
