DESCRIPTION:Join the Office of Research of Development (ORD) and NC TraCS d
 uring University Research Week to explore research opportunities at the in
 tersection of climate\, health\, and extreme weather. ORD is tracking a re
 cent emphasis at NIH on the relationship between health and climate\, foll
 owing the release of a Health and Extreme Weather highlighted topic\, anot
 her on time-sensitive research projects on environmental health\, and an N
 IH-NSF Research Award Program partnership.\n\n \n\nHear from NIEHS program
  staff\, learn about innovative research taking place across campus\, and 
 connect with collaborators for future research opportunities.\n\n \n\nHigh
 lights include:\n\nNIEHS program staff involved in developing the various 
 newly announced initiatives will be present to share the latest updates an
 d meet with faculty one-on-oneFaculty lightning talks will showcase UNC ex
 pertise\, ongoing projects\, and emerging research directions to build new
  collaborationsNetworking opportunities will build interdisciplinary conne
 ctions and explore potential collaborations \n\nRegister\n\n \n\nPlease re
 gister by October 19 to participate. If you are interested in presenting a
  5-minute lightning talk OR if you would like to request one of the limite
 d one-on-one meeting times with NIEHS program staff\, please contact Kelle
 y Cardone at kelley_cardone@unc.edu.
GEO:35.905771;-79.051242
LOCATION:Brinkhous-Bullitt Building\, 219
SUMMARY:UNC Research Connections: Health & Extreme Weather
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/unc-research-connections-healt
 h-extreme-weather
END:VEVENT
