  professor in the Department of History and the Bancroft-Prize winning aut
 hor of The Sewing Girl’s Tale\, moderated by Michael A. Betts II of High
  Point University\, followed by a concert by C. Leonard Raybon\, director 
 of choirs and a composer at Tulane University\, and UNC-Chapel Hill underg
 raduate and alumna performers in the UNC Department of Music\, featuring E
 . Katherine Hargrove of Colonial Williamsburg\, Mending Sampler: Lanah Saw
 yer and the Cost of Courage in Revolutionary America.
