BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/native-tree-planting-cornelius/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T120000
DTSTAMP:20261005T191205Z
CREATED:20261005T191204Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261005T191205Z
UID:10001824-1792832400-1792843200@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Native Tree Planting (Cornelius)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF Lake Norman Wildlife Chapter to plant native trees in Cornelius as part of North Carolina Wildlife Federation’s Clean and Green program. Back in April\, NCWF Lake Norman Wildlife Chapter and the Town of Cornelius hosted its annual Clean & Green trash cleanup event. Town staff and volunteers from the Society of Women Engineers\, Safe Harbor – Kings Point Marina\, and Lake Norman Wildlife took to the land and the lake to remove hundreds of pounds of trash and debris. \nNorth Carolina Wildlife Federation is committed to planting one native tree for every 25 pounds of trash collected statewide. Removing litter protects wildlife from possible entanglement\, strangulation\, and ingestion while improving water quality and removing toxins from the environment. \nThis year we will plant native trees at Bailey Road Park. Trees are the foundation of our terrestrial food webs\, and they provide critical nesting habitat for owls\, hawks\, songbirds\, and other wildlife. Please join us at Bailey Road Park for a morning of community and conservation. Stick around for pizza\, refreshments\, and a group photo at the end. \nVolunteers will work to prepare the existing holes before planting and mulching up to 80 native trees. \nChildren under 18 must be accompanied by a parent or guardian. \nPlease reach out to Billy Wilson\, President – Lake Norman Wildlife\, with questions at billy.wilson@LNWC.org\, or 704-675-2011\n \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/native-tree-planting-cornelius/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/BaileyRoadParkNativeTreePlanting.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:Defend Democracy Saturdays: Downtown Durham
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T113000
DTSTAMP:20261010T053253Z
UID:7vihpmeg1k6esqp5s5vsvq9hfe_R20260110T150000@google.com__20261024
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20251010T141601Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Saturday 
 from 10am-11:30am with signs to protect our democracy and protest the viol
 ations to our Constitution. We will meet at the YMCA at 218 West Morgan St
 .</p><p>We need to fight for our democracy and stop and prevent future cut
 s that are hurting many. Bring friends! Bring signs that show your concern
  or are a call to action. Please avoid triggering images like swastikas.</
 p><p>See you every Saturday morning engaging drivers &amp\; pedestrians in
  Downtown Durham!</p><p>Please join our Substack:<span> </span><a href="h
 ttps://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy">https
 ://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy</a></p><p>
 For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<span> </span><a href="https://www.mobilize
 .us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersf
 ordemocracy/</a></p><p><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfor
 democracy/event/842514/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocra
 cy/event/842514/</a> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260108T021307Z
LOCATION:218 W Morgan St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Nchumanities": "https://nchumanities.org/event/spellbound-at-mordecai/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:nchumanities
X-SOURCE:NC Humanities Council
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T140000
DTSTAMP:20260928T151629Z
CREATED:20260928T151629Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928T151629Z
UID:10001452-1792836000-1792850400@nchumanities.org
SUMMARY:Spellbound at Mordecai
DESCRIPTION:Magic and mayhem abound at Spellbound at Mordecai\, presented in partnership with Paper & Stars Studio!\nDecorate a pumpkin to take home\, shop for enchanting handmade items and treats\, and meet mysterious characters. Enjoy family-friendly stage performances\, inflatables\, crafts\, and more. Wear your best Halloween finery to enter the costume contest. Prizes will be awarded for best children’s costume and best group costume! \nJoin The Ghost Guild\, Inc. for their annual Haunted Mordecai presentation\, which includes immersive tours in the very locations where their data was collected. Reserve your tickets in advance on The Ghost Guild’s Eventbrite page or on a first-come\, first-served basis on the day of the event. \nThis is a family event full of spooky fun for children – no horror\, gore\, weapons\, or full masks\, please.
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/spellbound-at-mordecai/
LOCATION:Mordecai Historic Park\, 1 Mimosa Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27604\, United States
CATEGORIES:Humanities Sector Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2025_Spellbound-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
