BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group Gregg Museum Of Art Design": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/opening-celebration-of-grounded-by-maya-freelon"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_gregg_museum_of_art_design
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20261010T053316Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54100007281045
DTSTART:20261107T180000Z
DTEND:20261107T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun-filled afternoon at the Gregg Museum of Art &
  Design to celebrate the opening of Grounded by acclaimed artist Maya Free
 lon. \n\nDrawing on her signature use of delicate tissue paper\, Freelon t
 ransforms the galleries into an immersive environment that honors both fra
 gility and resilience. In Grounded\, the red clay and soil of North Caroli
 na become central materials and metaphors\, asking us to consider what it 
 means to create sanctuary in uncertain times and how the land itself holds
  memory\, pain\, and possibility.\n\nThe community celebration will includ
 e local organizations highlighting African American heritage and wellness\
 , along with special performances by Tre. Charles\, Johnny Lee Chapman III
 \, and NC State’s Panoramic Dance Project. \n\nYou are invited to Connec
 t. Celebrate. Get Grounded. Please read more about the timed activities be
 low.\n\nCelebration Program Schedule\n\n1 p.m. | Celebration Begins\n\nEnj
 oy ongoing activities throughout the museum and grounds from 1-5 p.m.\, in
 cluding a collaborative Tissue Paper Quilting activity inside the Grounded
  exhibition\, community organization tables\, a food truck and more. Compl
 imentary non-alcoholic beverages and light treats will be provided. \n\n1:
 15–1:45 p.m. | Panoramic Dance\nExperience a special performance choreog
 raphed by Christa Oliver and featuring NC State students. The performance 
 begins outside the museum’s main entrance\, inviting visitors to follow 
 the dancers into the galleries for a brief performance before moving toget
 her outdoors. Accessible seating will be available for visitors who need a
 ccommodations. The program is primarily designed for standing-room viewing
 . \n\n1:45–2:10 p.m. | Welcome and Opening Remarks with artist Maya Free
 lon\nOpening remarks with artist Maya Freelon\, Gregg Museum Director Sara
  Segerlin\, and special guests\, at the concert stage by the front lawn.\n
 \n2:15–3:45 p.m. | Tre. Charles concert at the Museum Lawn\nEnjoy an out
 door concert on the lawn featuring Tre. Charles and band.  Please feel fre
 e to bring a lawn chair or blanket.\n\n2:45–3 p.m. and 3:30–3:45 p.m. 
 | Spoken Word with Johnny Lee Chapman\nRaleigh Poet Laureate Johnny Lee Ch
 apman presents two intimate spoken word performances in Crafting Sanctuari
 es.\n\n3:45–4:15 p.m. | Panoramic Dance\nA second opportunity to experie
 nce Panoramic Dance with Christa Oliver and NC State students\, beginning 
 outside the museum entrance and moving through the galleries and outdoors.
  Accessible seating will be available for visitors who need accommodations
 . The program is primarily designed for standing-room viewing. \n\n5 p.m. 
 | Celebration Concludes \n\nParking: The Gregg Museum parking lot will be 
 closed for the celebration. Visitors may park in the Ferndell public parki
 ng lot or at Pullen Arts Center\, where parking is free on Saturdays. Thes
 e alternate parking locations are approximately 2–4 blocks from the muse
 um. Please visit the Gregg Museum website for additional parking informati
 on: https://gregg.arts.ncsu.edu/about/visit/alternate-parking-locations-fo
 r-the-gregg-museum/\n\nFree and open to the public. Please register for th
 e general event\, and feel free to drop in anytime between 1 and 5 p.m.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Opening Celebration of Grounded by Maya Freelon
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/opening-celebration-of-ground
 ed-by-maya-freelon
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
