BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardens": "https://gardens.duke.edu/event/a-festival-of-fabulous-mums-6/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardens
X-SOURCE:Sarah P. Duke Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T160000
DTSTAMP:20260915T130805Z
CREATED:20260706T123130Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T130805Z
UID:17496-1794132000-1794153600@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:A Festival of Fabulous Mums
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy an explosion of color this fall during A Festival of Fabulous Mums at Duke Gardens. Exhibition mums will create a dazzling floral display outdoors at the Ruth Mary Meyer Japanese Garden in the Culberson Asiatic Arboretum and inside the Doris Duke Center. Central Carolina Chrysanthemum Society members will be on hand to highlight the 13 classes of mums and answer questions. Children must be accompanied by an adult. \nFee: Free drop-in exhibit for all ages; no registration required. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Inside the Doris Duke Center and outdoors in the Ruth Mary Meyer Japanese Garden. \nAccessibility: This is a drop-in exhibit that takes place indoors in an area accessible via paved paths and outdoors on a combination of paved and unpaved paths with some uneven surfaces and moderate inclines.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/a-festival-of-fabulous-mums-6/
LOCATION:Sarah P. Duke Gardens\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27708\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs,Family programs,Festival of Fabulous Mums
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Hanley_Asiatic-Arboretum_Pine-Clouds-Mountain-Stream_chrysanthemum-Diane-Stokes_11-13-21-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Triangleland": "https://triangleland.org/event/get-wild-falling-for-trees"}
X-SOURCE-ID:triangleland
X-SOURCE:Triangle Land Conservancy
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T120000
DTSTAMP:20260917T192655Z
CREATED:20260917T192655Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260917T192655Z
UID:10000113-1794132000-1794139200@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Get Wild: FALLing for Trees!
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC for this family friendly exploration of the wonderful world of trees!\nTrail Guide Donna Agnew will lead families on a romp through Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve to explore the life cycle of trees\, go on a tree scavenger hunt\, search for cool bugs and plants\, and make nature leaf crowns! \n\nFilled with Umbrella Magnolias\, Sparklberry trees\, and so much more\, Old Creedmoor is the perfect spot for exploring trees. Perfect for kids ages 5+ and their grownups! This event is free\, but pre-registration is required:\n\n\n\nIf registration is full\, please email Meera Butalia at mbutalia@triangleland.org to be added to the waitlist.
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/get-wild-falling-for-trees
LOCATION:Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve\, 13509 Old Creedmoor Rd\, Wake Forest\, NC\, 27587\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardens": "https://gardens.duke.edu/event/festival-of-fabulous-mums-growing-fabulous-mums-with-joan-matthews/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardens
X-SOURCE:Sarah P. Duke Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T120000
DTSTAMP:20260915T130804Z
CREATED:20260908T205431Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T130804Z
UID:17907-1794135600-1794139200@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:Festival of Fabulous Mums: Growing Fabulous Mums with Joan Matthews
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a series of free demonstrations and workshops during the Festival of Fabulous Mums at Duke Gardens! In this session\, learn how to grow the spectacular chrysanthemums on display at the Festival of Fabulous Mums. See samples of chrysanthemums at various growth stages as you learn the basic horticultural elements involved in growing them. Learn about the 13 classes of mums\, how to obtain new plants and their requirements for soil\, light\, water and fertilizer. With this introduction\, you will be ready to grow these incredible blooms in your garden. \nAs a longtime chrysanthemum grower\, a National Chrysanthemum Society judge\, and former president of Central Carolina Chrysanthemum Society\, Joan Matthews presents engaging educational programs on the cultivation\, exhibition and history of chrysanthemums. \nThis series of free demonstrations and workshops will take place in the Pelham-Cullen Classroom inside the Barnes Welcome Center. No registration required. Seating is limited and available on a first-come\, first-served basis. Doors open 15 min before the scheduled start time.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/festival-of-fabulous-mums-growing-fabulous-mums-with-joan-matthews/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Pelham-Cullen Classroom in the Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs,Festival of Fabulous Mums
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Bodine_Asiatic-1859.jpg
END:VEVENT
