BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ackland-film-forum-nightcrawler-dan-gilroy-2014"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261010T052519Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54007493240432
DTSTART:20261110T003000Z
DTEND:20261110T020000Z
DESCRIPTION:Jake Gyllenhaal delivers a career-defining performance as an am
 bitious freelancer who prowls Los Angeles after dark in search of footage 
 for local television news. The city’s nocturnal landscape of police sire
 ns\, flashing lights\, and breaking stories becomes the backdrop for a mor
 dant examination of ambition\, competition\, and media culture in the twen
 ty-first century. \nThis film will be introduced by Kino Korner\, graduate
  student association. \nIt will be screened at 7:30 p.m. at The Lumina The
 ater (620 Market St\, Chapel Hill\, NC 27516). Tickets are free for all au
 dience members\, and registration is required via The Lumina’s webpage. 
 When this link is live\, click to reserve your free ticket. \nUNC-Chapel H
 ill students can receive CLE credit for attending by scanning the QR code 
 at the event. \n  \nAbout the Series: \nJoin the Ackland Film Forum this f
 all for Socially Charged Crime Thrillers: Snapshots of Social Anxiety\, a 
 series that accompanies the Ackland exhibition Care and Concern: Recent Ac
 quisitions of Modern and Contemporary Art. \nAs vehicles of social comment
 ary and stylistic bravura\, crime thrillers often register the pressures a
 nd contradictions of their historical moment. Across nearly half a century
 \, the films in this series stage encounters with political power\, public
  trust\, inequality\, and ambition through assassination plots\, botched r
 obberies\, and media-driven spectacle. \nFrom the crises of the late 1960s
  to the intensified media environments of the twenty-first century\, these
  works show how genre cinema can capture social anxiety in real time. Each
  film stands both as a gripping narrative and as a record of a world under
  strain\, where institutions falter and everyday life becomes fraught with
  conflict. \nThe Ackland Film Forum is co-organized by the Ackland Art Mus
 eum and UNC Film Studies\, housed in the UNC-Chapel Hill Department of Eng
 lish and Comparative Literature.
LOCATION:The Lumina Theater\, 620 Market Street\, Chapel Hill\, 27516\, Uni
 ted States
SUMMARY:Ackland Film Forum: "Nightcrawler" (Dan Gilroy\, 2014)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ackland-film-forum-nightcrawle
 r-dan-gilroy-2014
CATEGORIES:Exhibits
END:VEVENT
