UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54010440409872
DTSTART:20261111T160000Z
DTEND:20261111T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:This workshop\, led by University Library staff\, will explore 
 strategies for using AI more intentionally. We will discuss topics ranging
  from browser tracking to the role of AI tools in your everyday life. We w
 ill also introduce practical ways to take more control of when or how thos
 e tools are used\, how your data are collected and tracked\, and ways you 
 can opt out. At the end of the workshop\, we will share additional resourc
 es for learning more about AI and adopting a more mindful approach to AI i
 n our world.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the University Library an
 d will be led by librarians Dayna Durbin and Gracie Riehm.\n\n \n\nThis wo
 rkshop is being offered remotely via Zoom only. You can register through t
 he library calendar. Registrants will receive a Zoom link\; those on the w
 aitlist will not receive a Zoom link unless they are bumped up to a regist
 ered spot.\n\n \n\nAll registrants however\, will receive access to the me
 eting recording and resources.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Opting Out of Integrated AI
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/opting-out-of-ai
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
