BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/learning-from-electric-lady-presented-by-john-storyk-award-winning-studio-designer"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261010T052519Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53922906772973
DTSTART:20261201T223000Z
DTEND:20261202T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:“Learning from Electric Lady”\nNoted architect and acoustic
 ian John Storyk will be on campus for a presentation on his lifetime caree
 r for the professional audio and video recording community\, highlighting 
 his work in studio design\, including new projects and ideas about where t
 he studio design world is headed.\n\n \n\nA registered architect and acous
 tician\, John Storyk and wife Beth Walters are the founding partners of WS
 DG. The firm has provided acoustic and AV technology consulting and design
  services since the groundbreaking 1969 design of Jimi Hendrix’s Electri
 c Lady Studios in New York City.\n\n \n\nJohn received his architectural s
 tudies from Princeton and Columbia Universities. As an designer\, engineer
  and principal of WSDG he has been responsible for over 3000 world-class a
 udio/video production facilities\, including studios\, radio stations\, vi
 deo suites\, entertainment clubs and theaters. His work includes private s
 tudios for Whitney Houston\, Bob Marley\, Ace Frehley\, Stevie Wonder\, Pa
 ul Epworth\, Jack Antonoff\, Bruce Springsteen\, Alicia Keys\, J. Cole\, G
 reenday\, Harry Connick\, JR\, JZ and others. Professional audio video ins
 tallations include Soundshop (Nashville)\; Crawford Post (Atlanta)\; Talki
 ng House (San Francisco)\; Rue Boyer (Paris)\, Sony (LA)\, Spotify (LA)\; 
 Jungle Studios (NYC)\; KEXP Radio (Seatle)\; Jazz at Lincoln Center (NYC)\
 ; UCLA – Lani Hall (Los Angeles)\; and Berklee College of Music (Boston)
 .\n\n \n\nJohn is a member of the American Institute of Architects (AIA)\,
  Acoustical Society of America\, Audio Engineering Society (AES) and a fre
 quent contributor to AES convention papers and professional industry perio
 dicals. He is a frequent lecturer at schools throughout the nation and has
  established courses in acoustics at several universities\, including Berk
 lee College of Music\, where he is a long time adjunct professor of acoust
 ics and studio design.\n\n \n\nHe and the 60 person global WSDG team are a
  13-time winner of the NAMM TEC award for studio design.\n\n \n\nThis even
 t is free and open to the public. Students can earn CLE credit for attendi
 ng.
GEO:35.912607;-79.053261
LOCATION:Hill Hall\, Moeser Auditorium
SUMMARY:“Learning from Electric Lady\,” presented by John Storyk\, Awar
 d Winning Studio Designer
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/learning-from-electric-lady-pr
 esented-by-john-storyk-award-winning-studio-designer
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
