X-SOURCE-ID:ncbg
X-SOURCE:NC Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T153000
DTSTAMP:20261006T002036Z
CREATED:20261006T001751Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T002036Z
UID:10000875-1796475600-1796484600@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Almost Winter Forest Bathing Walk
DESCRIPTION:with Aimee Vandemark\, Certified Forest and Nature Therapy Guide \nForest Therapy (sometimes known as Forest Bathing or Shinrin-Yoku) broadly means taking in the forest atmosphere with all of one’s senses. Not simply a walk in the woods; it is the conscious and contemplative practice of being immersed in the sights\, sounds\, and smells of the forest. During your walk\, Aimee Vandemark will guide you through invitations to awaken your senses\, slow down\, be present\, and reconnect with the nature and rhythm of your surroundings. Minimum Age: 18 \nREGISTER HERE \nRegistration is managed by the program leader. \nRegistration deadline: Friday\, December 4 at 10 a.m.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/goodbye-to-fall-forest-bathing-walk/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Health and Wellbeing
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=North Carolina Botanical Garden 100 Old Mason Farm Road Chapel Hill NC 27517 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=100 Old Mason Farm Road:geo:-79.031939,35.901081
END:VEVENT
