BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_lgbtqcenterofdurham_org_qb71v8n48d0a304sq7dtm89f84
SUMMARY:Free & Confidential HIV/STI Testing 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261224T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261224T150000
DTSTAMP:20261010T053301Z
UID:7pe8achei4d9o6djftcff8o2fe_R20260723T170000@google.com__20261224
SEQUENCE:2
CREATED:20260629T193931Z
DESCRIPTION:Durham County’s “I Take Testing Seriously” Program (ITTS
 ) works with community partners and members alike to decrease rates of HIV
 \, Syphilis\, Hepatitis C\, Gonorrhea\, and Chlamydia. Our public health e
 ducators provide comprehensive sexual health services anywhere in Durham C
 ounty.<br><br>When folx attend testing services through the LGBTQ Center o
 f Durham\, they are able to receive: free and confidential HIV/STI screeni
 ngs\, PrEP referrals as needed\, and confidential counseling on next steps
 .<br><br>Specimens are sent to the NC State Lab  for testing where a 4<s
 up>th</sup> generation test is used.<br><br>Access to free barriers (inte
 rnal\, external) and lubrication is always readily available.<br><br>Our t
 ester can also answer questions about PrEP and provide initial steps in th
 e County's Quick Start program for PrEP. Stop in today!<br><br>Are you not
  ready to test? Stop in for an informational session.  All questions welc
 ome.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260801T202349Z
LOCATION:114 Hunt St\, Durham\, NC 27701\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:LGBTQ Center of Durham
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group African American Cultural Center": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/you-are-here-geolocating-the-self-through-the-familiar-in-the-midst-of-the-unfamiliar-exhibition"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_african_american_cultural_center
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20261010T053315Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53550588357574
DTSTART:20261224T150000Z
DTEND:20261224T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center to experience ariana 
 Farquharson's You Are Here: Geolocating the Self through the Familiar in t
 he Midst of the Unfamiliar. The exhibition is a speculative\, immersive wo
 rld-building study that invites guests to explore (geo)locating self and h
 ome amid a rapidly and frequently changing post-pandemic “new” world. 
 It will be on display in the art gallery at the African American Cultural 
 Center from Oct. 28\, 2026\, to  Feb. 28\, 2027. A behind-the-scenes look 
 at the exhibition is set for Nov. 11.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (218
 )
SUMMARY:You Are Here Exhibition
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/you-are-here-geolocating-the-
 self-through-the-familiar-in-the-midst-of-the-unfamiliar-exhibition
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
