BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_enoriver_org_9u7o786v1jlk6heq5cp3k1gr1k
SUMMARY:ERA & ERSP: First Day Hike on the Eno
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270101T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270101T163000
DTSTAMP:20261010T053257Z
UID:4jjojno2b1g88jfc0fv8a7ol30@google.com__20270101
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20210803T152701Z
DESCRIPTION:Kick off the New Year with a hike on the Eno! An annual tradit
 ion that started in 1971\, hike alongside friends and family at Eno River 
 State Park to start the new year together.<br><b><br></b><br><b>When:</b>
  2:00pm on Wednesday\, January 1st 2025<br><b>Where: </b>Eno River State 
 Park\, Cox Mountain Trailhead\, 6101 Cole Mill Rd\, Durham NC<br><b>What t
 o expect when you arrive: </b>The event begins at 2:00pm\, but please plan
  to arrive early as parking fills up closer to the start of the event. Par
 k Rangers and volunteers will be on-site to assist with parking. Please fo
 llow their instructions. Check-in at the Eno River Association table locat
 ed at the end of the parking lot near the Fews Ford picnic shelter.<br><b>
 Hikes: </b>At 2:00pm\, gather in the Fews Ford picnic area at the Cox Moun
 tain Trailhead for a welcome message from the Eno River Association and En
 o River State Park Superintendent. There will be two hike options led by a
  hike leader - a short hike along Buckquarter Creek Trail (about 2.5 miles
 ) and a long hike along Cox Mountain Trail (about 4.5 miles). After comple
 ting your hike\, join us for hot cocoa and conversation at the Fews Ford p
 icnic shelter back at the trailhead.<br><br>See you there!!
LAST-MODIFIED:20251105T152730Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-APPLE-TRAVEL-ADVISORY-BEHAVIOR:AUTOMATIC
X-SOURCE:Eno River Association
