BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/earspace-cmm-26-27"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261010T052519Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53825469749193
DTSTART:20270116T003000Z
DTEND:20270116T013000Z
DESCRIPTION:FEATURING\n\nearspace\n\nearspace is an ensemble consisting of 
 violin\, viola\, cello\, flute\, oboe\, clarinet\, piano\, and percussion 
 that performs a combination of conducted and unconducted chamber music of 
 a wide variety of scopes. Passionate producers\, the ensemble is dedicated
  to both commissioning new\, immersive works and amplifying rarely-perform
 ed gems of the repertoire. Founded in North Carolina\, the group is now ba
 sed across the US and performs regularly around the east coast\, collabora
 ting with organizations including the Southern Exposure New Music Series\,
  Towson University\, Duke University\, UNC Chapel Hill\, the Peabody Insti
 tute\, Asheville Ballet\, Carolina Performing Arts\, and others.\n\nThe en
 semble seeks to expose the inherent potentials within every moment and spa
 ce\, cultivating visceral reactions unique to every manifestation. Through
  their projects\, they explore the extremities of contemporary performance
  and work to bring audiences closer to the music they experience.\n\n \n\n
 PROGRAM\n\nTBA\n\n \n\nPARKING\n\nPlease plan to arrive early as parking o
 n campus can be tricky. Learn more about parking and directions to UNC-Cha
 pel Hill’s campus.\n\nThis performance is part of the 2026-2027 Conversa
 tions in Modern Music series and is funded by the Jaroslav F. and Barbara 
 S. Hulka Fund for Music in the Chapel Hill community.
GEO:35.912607;-79.053261
LOCATION:Hill Hall\, Moeser Auditorium
SUMMARY:earspace | CMM 26-27
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/earspace-cmm-26-27
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
